00:30:09.170 --> 00:30:10.010
So--

00:30:10.010 --> 00:30:11.650
EJAL BRACHA: OK, say no more.

00:30:11.650 --> 00:30:14.620
Tell me a little about-- because
another HIPAA-approved product

00:30:14.620 --> 00:30:17.080
is the Citrix ADC.

00:30:17.080 --> 00:30:20.550
And that's one of the
reasons you chose it.

00:30:20.550 --> 00:30:21.990
ULRIK CHRISTENSEN: The ADC--

00:30:21.990 --> 00:30:26.040
the reason why we
looked at the ADC is--

00:30:26.040 --> 00:30:27.840
one of the things
is that we need

00:30:27.840 --> 00:30:35.640
to make sure that the
application itself is safe,

00:30:35.640 --> 00:30:38.910
it's secure, and the data that
is being put in there is safe.

00:30:41.520 --> 00:30:45.880
And also, we need to have
some kind of user control.

00:30:45.880 --> 00:30:52.890
So we use the ADC to
ask different IDPs--

00:30:52.890 --> 00:30:57.390
it can be from a company,
it can be from Google,

00:30:57.390 --> 00:30:58.440
it can be from--

00:30:58.440 --> 00:31:03.016
you can even use Facebook,
if you want to, but just--

00:31:03.016 --> 00:31:10.540
so we can control which
users have access to this.

00:31:10.540 --> 00:31:14.850
So if we have someone that
comes up to us and says,

00:31:14.850 --> 00:31:16.670
we would really like to--

00:31:16.670 --> 00:31:24.858
we would like to
try your DRP system,

00:31:24.858 --> 00:31:29.410
we can integrate with
whatever user IDP

00:31:29.410 --> 00:31:31.300
that they're actually using.

00:31:31.300 --> 00:31:35.260
So yeah, that's one of--
that's some of the reasons

00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:38.470
why we chose the Citrix ADC.

00:31:38.470 --> 00:31:44.120
Another one is that Citrix has
introduced something called

00:31:44.120 --> 00:31:47.200
the Citrix ingress controller.

00:31:47.200 --> 00:31:53.360
Now, each-- we have
a number of what

00:31:53.360 --> 00:31:57.890
is called pods on Kubernetes
running our web application.

00:31:57.890 --> 00:32:02.960
So we have the CPX--

00:32:02.960 --> 00:32:09.680
Citrix ADC CPX load
balancing the different pods

00:32:09.680 --> 00:32:11.870
on Kubernetes.

00:32:11.870 --> 00:32:13.760
And then we have a VPX--

00:32:13.760 --> 00:32:19.950
Citrix ADC VPX that are load
balancing the different CPXs.

00:32:19.950 --> 00:32:22.550
And what happens is that, if--

00:32:22.550 --> 00:32:28.520
let's say, we run up
four or five pods,

00:32:28.520 --> 00:32:33.440
the Citrix ingress
controller automatically

00:32:33.440 --> 00:32:37.740
puts the configuration from the
second tier to the first tier

00:32:37.740 --> 00:32:38.660
ADC.

00:32:38.660 --> 00:32:45.290
So if you have something
that breaks and the cluster

00:32:45.290 --> 00:32:50.510
needs to spin up a
new part, that change

00:32:50.510 --> 00:32:56.582
will automatically be
configured to the ADC.

00:32:56.582 --> 00:33:00.840
So that gives a
great way to deliver

00:33:00.840 --> 00:33:04.631
a very reliable service.

00:33:04.631 --> 00:33:06.540
Yep.

00:33:06.540 --> 00:33:08.951
EJAL BRACHA: So
basically you can--

00:33:08.951 --> 00:33:11.030
it can handle--
whether you spin up

00:33:11.030 --> 00:33:16.250
20 containers or 50 containers
or 2,000 containers,

00:33:16.250 --> 00:33:18.590
it will still manage
each container

00:33:18.590 --> 00:33:20.810
as a separate environment.

00:33:20.810 --> 00:33:24.770
And it will make sure that
your medical data is protected

00:33:24.770 --> 00:33:26.210
within that container.

00:33:26.210 --> 00:33:27.500
ULRIK CHRISTENSEN: Yes.

00:33:27.500 --> 00:33:29.956
